RIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"vLLM supports a KV cache quantization method known as `fp8-per-token-head`, though this is currently supported only by Triton attention.\n\nThe `fp8-per-token-head` KV cache quantization generates an FP32 scale for each head, offering finer granularity compared to `fp8-per-tensor` quantization.\n\nTo facilitate KV cache management, the scales are stored inline within the KV cache and aligned to 16 bytes (ensuring compatibility with `cp.async`).\n\nPlease add support for `fp8-per-token-head` KV cache quantization to FlashInfer.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/issues/3617/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/issues/3617/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}